  "id": "summating-potential",
  "term": "summating potential",
  "definition": "Summating potential is a waveform peak in click-evoked electrocochleography that reflects activity generated by hair cells in the cochlea. In this source, it is considered alongside the action potential from cochlear neurons, and the SP/AP ratio is used as a possible sign of hidden hearing loss related to selective neural damage.",
